t-code (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A debugger: gdb over DAP, breakpoints (with conditions), F5 / stepping,
    the Run and Debug panel (variables, watch, call stack, breakpoints),
    values under the pointer, a Disassembly View.
  * Quick fixes (Ctrl+.), Go to Symbol in File, Switch Source / Header, uses
    of the symbol at the cursor highlighted, #if branches left out dimmed.
  * Code folding and sticky scroll.
  * Color themes with previews, a square look, settings.ini and hand-editable
    theme files.
  * Panels that move between docks, a title bar button per panel, Open in New
    Window.
  * Right-click menus everywhere; Source Control commit details; comparisons
    open at the first change.
  * A save conflict bar; Run for Python, JavaScript, Rust, Go, Java and other
    projects.

 -- suacayipkisi <ufukdenizcaglayan@gmail.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0300

t-code (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Files panel is a native folder tree (GtkListView) instead of a
    terminal file manager: lazy folders, git colors, drag and drop, create /
    rename / delete / copy / move.
  * Temporary tabs (a click in the file tree previews a file), and a comparison is one tab.
  * Indentation from .editorconfig, .clang-format or the file itself, shown
    and changeable per project in the status bar.
  * clangd can be restarted from the Command Palette; a status bar hint when
    no compile flags are found.
  * Smarter Enter after an opening bracket, double click selects a name, other
    occurrences of a selected name are highlighted and marked beside the
    minimap.
  * Tab moves between a completed function's parameters.

 -- suacayipkisi <ufukdenizcaglayan@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300

t-code (0.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Editor tabs are GtkSourceView 5 views instead of micro terminals, with an
    in-process clangd client: problems underlined, completion, parameter
    hints, hover, go to definition, references, rename, formatting, semantic
    colors.
  * Find and replace bar, closing brackets and quotes, line commands, indent
    guides, a minimap marking problems, git's changes in the gutter.
  * Side-by-side comparisons stay aligned and scroll together.
  * Files, Source Control, Search and the shell can be moved between 12 docks.
  * Native Markdown preview (md4c in a text view): no WebKit.
  * Less memory: one clangd with at most five open documents, freed heap
    returned to the system, no process per editor.

 -- suacayipkisi <ufukdenizcaglayan@gmail.com>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300

t-code (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Much less memory and CPU: editors start when their tab is first shown,
    hidden editors stay idle, clangd runs with two malloc arenas, the Markdown
    preview's network process exits with the last preview.
  * Opening t-code no longer flashes clipboard windows or clears the clipboard.
  * Tests for the shared language servers, including a heap growth check.

